02:34:40.010 --> 02:34:43.640
I still have my heirloom.

02:34:43.640 --> 02:34:44.640
You make me sick.

02:34:44.640 --> 02:34:49.690
Why did you ever have to leave that crazy house?

02:34:49.690 --> 02:34:56.410
Blessed be the pure in mind, for they shall find peace.

02:34:56.410 --> 02:34:58.030
And you are a coward, sir.

02:34:58.030 --> 02:34:59.070
What?

02:34:59.070 --> 02:35:00.000
Why are you...

02:35:01.340 --> 02:35:05.240
brave aren't you since Masterson no longer has a gun. Let go of me. Do you want to lose

02:35:05.240 --> 02:35:09.240
your job? I haven't had the opportunity to tell you yet, but I quit when we went out

02:35:09.240 --> 02:35:09.880
there in your orders.

02:35:33.100 --> 02:35:34.300
You brought Masterson?

02:35:34.300 --> 02:35:36.650
Yes, he's here.

02:35:36.650 --> 02:35:38.670
Good, we found him at last.

02:35:38.670 --> 02:35:41.500
What about the others?

02:35:41.500 --> 02:35:47.360
Well, I have something in mind for the girl and the pilot, the other I shall dispose of.

02:35:47.360 --> 02:35:53.240
Wolf?

02:37:03.770 --> 02:37:04.390
Waceless air.

02:37:05.080 --> 02:37:06.150
Who is dead?

02:37:06.810 --> 02:37:07.130
Yeah.

02:37:07.970 --> 02:37:11.560
You murdered him.

02:37:14.890 --> 02:37:19.660
Fresh.

02:37:20.050 --> 02:37:20.590
Back on me.

02:37:22.630 --> 02:37:23.990
And put one more water on that fire.

02:37:24.090 --> 02:37:24.250
Quick.

02:37:25.800 --> 02:37:27.830
Just keep it moving, Marine.

02:37:28.320 --> 02:37:29.820
Remember, we haven't seen him yet.

02:37:30.120 --> 02:37:32.000
- Aren't you afraid, Grant?

02:37:32.000 --> 02:37:33.440
- I'm scared stiff.

02:37:33.440 --> 02:37:37.150
- If you're frightened, what do you call him?

02:37:37.150 --> 02:37:38.660
- I can't stand it.

02:37:38.660 --> 02:37:41.100
I'm getting out of here.

02:37:41.100 --> 02:37:42.350
Don't be a fool.

02:37:42.350 --> 02:37:44.400
The only thing keeping your back is on fire.

02:38:25.690 --> 02:38:27.680
We'll discover consciousness in a moment or so.

02:38:27.680 --> 02:38:29.220
It'll be perfectly sane again.

02:38:30.570 --> 02:38:37.470
fortunate he left us in such a state before understand that he committed to an asylum

02:38:37.470 --> 02:38:47.810
attempted to kill tarantella grant look it's a dancer from the cafe i saw him kill her amazing

02:38:47.810 --> 02:38:58.920
the durability of my creations dr aranja that's spanish for spider we meet again doctor again

02:38:58.920 --> 02:39:00.000
did i leave here

02:39:01.690 --> 02:39:04.510
I seem to remember vaguely that...

02:39:04.510 --> 02:39:09.180
Yes, you escaped for a doctor, and you led us a married chase recovering you.

02:39:09.390 --> 02:39:11.810
Why? Why not just kill me? Why bring me back?

02:39:12.770 --> 02:39:14.810
Unfortunately, I still need your help.

02:39:15.410 --> 02:39:18.670
I'll give you one more chance to change your mind.

02:39:19.360 --> 02:39:22.220
No, never. Nothing you can do will ever make me a party to this.

02:39:23.060 --> 02:39:23.500
Carantella.

02:39:24.520 --> 02:39:26.140
No, you're not going to torture him anymore.

02:39:30.160 --> 02:39:44.530
A few moments this will explode and destroy you and me and all of your terrible creations.

02:39:44.530 --> 02:39:48.030
Doctor, you're a man of science! You wouldn't destroy the greatest achievement of science!

02:39:48.030 --> 02:39:51.040
Scientist? Yes, but I'm a human being too and that's where we differ.

02:39:51.040 --> 02:39:54.040
You two have got a chance. Through that door, down the corridor on the rock. Hurry!

02:39:54.040 --> 02:39:56.040
Who is he? What is this place?

02:39:56.040 --> 02:39:59.040
A brilliant madman. Hurry, there are only seconds left. What about you?

02:39:59.040 --> 02:40:00.000
Throw down, you go!

02:40:01.280 --> 02:40:07.460
your creations can grow a new arm or leg

02:40:07.460 --> 02:40:09.330
but nothing can survive fire

02:40:09.330 --> 02:40:25.140
I moved and staggered across that desert

02:40:25.140 --> 02:40:26.670
before he found us

02:40:26.670 --> 02:40:29.430
well

02:40:30.190 --> 02:40:34.610
That's about the story, believe it or not.

02:40:34.610 --> 02:40:35.640
Grant!

02:40:35.640 --> 02:40:39.460
How do you feel, honey?

02:40:39.460 --> 02:40:41.490
Alright, I guess.

02:40:41.490 --> 02:40:46.610
I've just been telling them our story, they don't buy it.

02:40:46.610 --> 02:40:50.280
How do you think he did?

02:40:50.280 --> 02:40:51.600
It's verdad.

02:40:51.600 --> 02:40:53.570
That's the truth.

02:40:53.570 --> 02:40:57.520
Now don't worry about it, you're gonna be alright in a couple of days.

02:40:57.520 --> 02:40:59.760
Just a little too much sun on the bare head.

02:41:00.830 --> 02:41:07.870
Anybody thinks I'm going to load one of my trucks with oil and send it up on top of a mountain to burn a bunch of imaginary spiders?

02:41:08.590 --> 02:41:10.780
Yes, you're right, Dan.

02:41:11.490 --> 02:41:16.030
Common sense tells you there isn't anything to his story, doesn't it?

02:41:16.710 --> 02:41:19.090
Giant spiders on a desert mesa.

02:41:20.200 --> 02:41:20.760
Fantastic.

02:41:22.060 --> 02:41:24.000
Pepe is just a superstitious native.

02:41:24.930 --> 02:41:30.000
True, no one has ever been on Sapa Mesa, but it's just like everything.

02:41:30.000 --> 02:42:00.000
other bit of table land not a thing different about it it's time to say good night we sincerely

02:42:00.030 --> 02:42:04.570
appreciate your patronage and hope we've succeeded in bringing you an enjoyable evening of

02:42:04.570 --> 02:42:09.340
entertainment. Please drive home carefully and come back again soon. Good night.
